%%meta name: Hospital Management System
%%meta kind: erd
%%meta version: 1.0.0
%%meta description: A hospital information system covering the whole of a patient's contact with the hospital. It holds the master patient record and the insurance policies attached to it; departments, wards and beds; the staff who work in them, and the doctors and nurses among them. Around those sits the clinical record: appointments that become encounters, and encounters that carry clinical notes, vital signs, diagnoses and procedures. Orders flow out of an encounter — prescriptions and their items, lab orders and their results, imaging orders and the radiologist's report — and each has a lifecycle of its own that the application enforces rather than describes. An admission takes a bed out of the pool and gives it back on discharge. Billing turns what was done into invoice lines priced from a chargeable-item catalogue, applies the insurance policy, and settles the balance against payments. Pharmacy and consumable stock is tracked through inventory items, suppliers and stock transactions, and an item that falls to its reorder level raises a replenishment of its own.
