    %%field Department.name help: The department's name as the hospital uses it — Cardiology, Radiology, Pathology. Unique, because two departments with one name is how a patient is sent to the wrong place.
    %%field Department.code help: The short code that appears on forms and reports, such as CARD.
    %%field Department.department_type help: What kind of unit this is. Decides whether it holds wards and beds, or only sees outpatients.
    %%field Department.doctor_id help: The consultant who runs the department. Named plainly rather than `head_doctor_id`, because the generator resolves a reference from the column name and `head_doctor_id` resolves to nothing. Left empty while a department is between heads.
    %%field Department.phone_extension help: The internal number the switchboard puts calls through on.
    %%field Department.floor help: Which floor of the building to find it on.
    %%field Department.is_active help: Untick when a department closes rather than deleting it — the encounters it managed must still resolve.
    %%field Department.department_type enum: DepartmentType
    %%index Department(department_type, is_active)
    %%rbac role:hospital_manager|administrator on Department.update
    %%rbac role:hospital_manager|administrator on Department.create

    %%field Ward.name help: What the ward is called on the signage and in conversation — Coronary Care, Ward 3B. Unique, because a patient sent to the wrong ward of the same name is a real incident.
    %%field Ward.code help: The short code used on bed boards and transfer notes, such as CCU.
    %%field Ward.department_id help: The department that runs this ward.
    %%field Ward.ward_type help: What kind of ward it is. Decides which patients may be admitted here and what level of nursing is required.
    %%field Ward.bed_capacity help: How many beds this ward is commissioned for. A gap between this and the number of bed records means beds were added or closed without the establishment being updated.
    %%field Ward.floor help: Which floor to find it on. Used by porters moving patients.
    %%field Ward.phone_extension help: The nurses' station number.
    %%field Ward.is_active help: Untick when a ward closes rather than deleting it — past admissions must still resolve to somewhere.
    %%field Ward.ward_type enum: WardType
    %%index Ward(department_id, is_active)
    %%index Ward(ward_type)
    %%rbac role:doctor|nurse|ward_manager|receptionist|hospital_manager|administrator on Ward.read
    %%rbac role:ward_manager|hospital_manager|administrator on Ward.update
    %%rbac role:ward_manager|hospital_manager|administrator on Ward.create

    %%field Bed.bed_code help: The hospital-wide identifier, ward code and number together, such as CCU-04. Unique across the hospital, because a bed board showing two beds called 4 is a bed board nobody trusts.
    %%field Bed.bed_number help: The number on the bed itself, unique only within its ward.
    %%field Bed.ward_id help: The ward this bed stands in.
    %%field Bed.bed_type help: What the bed is equipped for. An admission may only take a bed whose type suits it.
    %%field Bed.status help: Where the bed is in its cycle. Driven by the bed occupancy workflow rather than typed in.
    %%field Bed.last_cleaned_at help: When housekeeping last turned it round. Empty on a bed that has never been used.
    %%field Bed.is_active help: Untick when a bed is decommissioned rather than deleting it — past admissions must still resolve to the bed they were in.
    %%field Bed.bed_type enum: BedType
    %%field Bed.status enum: BedStatus
    %%index Bed(ward_id, status)
    %%index Bed(bed_type, status)
    %%rbac role:doctor|nurse|ward_manager|hospital_manager|administrator on Bed.read
    %%rbac role:ward_manager|hospital_manager|administrator on Bed.update
    %%rbac role:ward_manager|hospital_manager|administrator on Bed.create

    %%field Staff.staff_number help: The payroll and badge number. Unique, and the identifier used on anything printed.
    %%field Staff.first_name help: Given name, as it should appear on screen and on a signed note.
    %%field Staff.last_name help: Family name.
    %%field Staff.work_email help: Where work reaches them, and the address they sign in with.
    %%field Staff.phone help: Contact number — a bleep or a mobile.
    %%field Staff.department_id help: The department that employs them.
    %%field Staff.staff_role help: What this person does, which decides what the application lets them see and do. The values match the roles named in the access rules.
    %%field Staff.job_title help: The title on their contract, finer-grained than the role — Senior Staff Nurse against a role of nurse.
    %%field Staff.hired_on help: When they joined.
    %%field Staff.is_active help: Untick when someone leaves rather than deleting them — every note, order and result they signed must still resolve to a person, for years.
    %%field Staff.staff_role enum: StaffRole
    %%index Staff(department_id, is_active)
    %%index Staff(staff_role)
    %%rbac role:hospital_manager|administrator on Staff.update
    %%rbac role:hospital_manager|administrator on Staff.create

    %%field Doctor.staff_id help: The staff record this doctor is. Unique, because one person is one doctor.
    %%field Doctor.registration_number help: The number on the professional register they are licensed under. Unique, and the thing an audit checks.
    %%field Doctor.specialty help: The field they practise in. Decides which encounters and bookings reach them.
    %%field Doctor.qualification help: Their qualifications as they should appear on a letter — MBBS, FRCP.
    %%field Doctor.is_consultant help: Whether they hold consultant responsibility. A consultant may sign off work a junior cannot.
    %%field Doctor.accepts_new_patients help: Untick to keep them off the booking screen without deactivating the staff record.
    %%field Doctor.specialty enum: DoctorSpecialty
    %%index Doctor(specialty, accepts_new_patients)
    %%rbac role:hospital_manager|administrator on Doctor.update
    %%rbac role:hospital_manager|administrator on Doctor.create

    %%field Nurse.staff_id help: The staff record this nurse is. Unique, because one person is one nurse.
    %%field Nurse.registration_number help: The number on the nursing register they are licensed under.
    %%field Nurse.grade help: Their nursing grade, which decides what they may do unsupervised and what needs countersigning.
    %%field Nurse.home_ward_id help: The ward they normally work on. Left empty for bank and float staff, who have none.
    %%field Nurse.shift_pattern help: Which shifts they normally work. Not a roster — it is what a ward manager filters on when looking for cover.
    %%field Nurse.grade enum: NurseGrade
    %%field Nurse.shift_pattern enum: ShiftPattern
    %%index Nurse(home_ward_id, grade)
    %%rbac role:hospital_manager|ward_manager|administrator on Nurse.update
    %%rbac role:hospital_manager|ward_manager|administrator on Nurse.create

    %%field Patient.medical_record_number help: The hospital's own patient identifier, on every wristband, chart and label. Generated on registration and never reused.
    %%field Patient.national_health_number help: The national identifier where the patient has one. Left empty for an emergency admission that arrives without it.
    %%field Patient.first_name help: Given name, as it should be spoken to them and printed.
    %%field Patient.last_name help: Family name.
    %%field Patient.date_of_birth help: Used to identify the patient alongside their name, and to decide paediatric and geriatric pathways.
    %%field Patient.gender help: As the patient states it.
    %%field Patient.blood_group help: Recorded once typed. Empty until a sample has been taken.
    %%field Patient.phone help: The number to reach them on.
    %%field Patient.email help: Where appointment reminders and letters go.
    %%field Patient.address_line help: Street address.
    %%field Patient.city help: Town or city.
    %%field Patient.postcode help: Postcode, which is also how catchment reporting is done.
    %%field Patient.emergency_contact_name help: Who to call if the patient cannot speak for themselves.
    %%field Patient.emergency_contact_phone help: The number to call them on.
    %%field Patient.known_allergies help: Allergies and adverse reactions, in the words they were reported in. Read before prescribing.
    %%field Patient.registered_on help: When this record was first created.
    %%field Patient.is_deceased help: Marks the record closed to new activity while leaving every past encounter intact. Records are closed, never deleted.
    %%field Patient.gender enum: Gender
    %%field Patient.blood_group enum: BloodGroup
    %%index Patient(last_name, date_of_birth)
    %%index Patient(medical_record_number) unique
