    %%field LabOrder.order_number help: The laboratory's own number for this request, printed on every specimen label and quoted on the result. Generated on saving, never typed.
    %%field LabOrder.encounter_id help: The clinical contact the test was requested during.
    %%field LabOrder.ordered_by_id help: The member of staff responsible for the request, and the person a critical result is escalated to.
    %%field LabOrder.test_code help: The laboratory's code for the test requested.
    %%field LabOrder.test_name help: The test in words, as it appears on the request and the report.
    %%field LabOrder.specimen_type help: What has to be collected. Decides the container, and whether the request can be met at all.
    %%field LabOrder.priority help: How fast the laboratory must turn it round. A stat request goes to the top of the worklist.
    %%field LabOrder.status help: Where the request has got to, from asked for to resulted. Driven by the lifecycle.
    %%field LabOrder.is_escalated help: Set by the escalation workflow when a critical value comes back, so the worklist shows which requests someone still has to be told about.
    %%field LabOrder.ordered_at help: When the request was raised.
    %%field LabOrder.collected_at help: When the specimen was actually taken. Empty until it is, and the gap between this and the order time is the collection delay a ward is measured on.
    %%field LabOrder.clinical_details help: Why the test was requested. The laboratory needs it to interpret the value, not merely to report it.
    %%field LabOrder.specimen_type enum: SpecimenType
    %%field LabOrder.priority enum: OrderPriority
    %%field LabOrder.status enum: LabOrderStatus
    %%index LabOrder(status, priority)
    %%index LabOrder(encounter_id, ordered_at)
    %%rbac role:doctor|nurse|lab_technician|billing_clerk|hospital_manager|administrator on LabOrder.read
    %%rbac role:doctor|nurse on LabOrder.create
    %%rbac role:doctor|nurse|lab_technician on LabOrder.update
    %%rbac role:administrator on LabOrder.delete

    %%field LabResult.lab_order_id help: The request this value answers.
    %%field LabResult.analyte help: What was measured — haemoglobin, sodium, C-reactive protein. One order commonly produces several.
    %%field LabResult.value_numeric help: The measured value, where the test produces a number. Empty for a test that reports words.
    %%field LabResult.value_text help: The result in words, where the test produces no number — an organism named, or positive and negative. Empty for a numeric test.
    %%field LabResult.unit help: The unit the numeric value is in. A number without its unit is not a result.
    %%field LabResult.reference_low help: The bottom of the normal range this value is read against.
    %%field LabResult.reference_high help: The top of the normal range this value is read against.
    %%field LabResult.abnormal_flag help: How the value reads against its range. A critical flag escalates rather than merely colouring the row.
    %%field LabResult.verified_by_id help: The laboratory member of staff who verified the value. Empty until someone has, and an unverified result is not clinically actionable.
    %%field LabResult.verified_at help: When it was verified.
    %%field LabResult.resulted_at help: When the analyser produced the value.
    %%field LabResult.abnormal_flag enum: AbnormalFlag
    %%index LabResult(lab_order_id, resulted_at)
    %%index LabResult(abnormal_flag)
