    %%field ImagingOrder.order_number help: The imaging department's own number for this request, quoted on the study and the report. Generated on saving, never typed.
    %%field ImagingOrder.encounter_id help: The clinical contact the study was requested during.
    %%field ImagingOrder.ordered_by_id help: The member of staff responsible for the request, and the person a critical finding is escalated to.
    %%field ImagingOrder.modality help: What kind of imaging is being asked for. Decides which room and which equipment the study is booked into.
    %%field ImagingOrder.body_part help: What is to be imaged, in the words the request was written in.
    %%field ImagingOrder.priority help: How fast the study is needed. Same vocabulary as a laboratory request, deliberately.
    %%field ImagingOrder.status help: Where the request has got to, from asked for to reported. Driven by the lifecycle.
    %%field ImagingOrder.contrast_used help: Whether contrast was given. It changes the preparation, the safety checks and the price.
    %%field ImagingOrder.is_escalated help: Set by the escalation workflow when a critical finding is reported, so the worklist shows which studies someone still has to be told about.
    %%field ImagingOrder.ordered_at help: When the request was raised.
    %%field ImagingOrder.scheduled_for help: When the study is booked for. Empty until it is booked.
    %%field ImagingOrder.performed_at help: When the study was actually carried out. Empty until it is.
    %%field ImagingOrder.clinical_question help: The question the study is meant to answer. A radiologist reports against this; without it the report is a description rather than an answer.
    %%field ImagingOrder.modality enum: ImagingModality
    %%field ImagingOrder.priority enum: OrderPriority
    %%field ImagingOrder.status enum: ImagingOrderStatus
    %%index ImagingOrder(status, priority)
    %%index ImagingOrder(encounter_id, ordered_at)
    %%index ImagingOrder(modality, scheduled_for)
